<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sierre</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Siders</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sierre is a town in the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valais">Valais</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> at the boundary between French and German speech. It was one of the seven tenths (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zenden">Zenden</a>) that governed the Republic of the Valais from the 17th century until 1798. Its surroundings are among the main wine-growing areas of Switzerland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sierre.jpg" alt="Sierre" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Template:Bild-picswiss · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sierre-Lac.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
